    <item>
      <title>Far-right slows energy transition</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41893-026-01974-w</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Sustainability, Published online: 30 October 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41893-026-01974-w"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41893-026-01974-w&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Political identity is known to shape climate attitudes, but its effect on real-world adoption of clean technologies has been unclear. Now, data from Germany show that rising far-right support slows the uptake of rooftop solar and electric cars. However, these effects are not large enough to stall the transition.</content:encoded>
